  "before_native_query_obligations": [
    "Freeze exact source adapter and source certificate/accepted-decision pins; independently compare all source rows and occurrence names with no producer expected trace as authority.",
    "Freeze exact five-field native request and original-vs-extended theory distinction. Reject duplicate JSON keys, malformed command fields, changed target, extra axioms or schemas, lost duplicate license, and row/reference drift.",
    "Independently reconstruct fixed protocol/theory/target and free blocks/proof postfix words in exact order. Require blocks empty; exact three fixed and two free decoded trees; parser frame delimiters, finite atom alphabet and no prefix/tail injection.",
    "Use unchanged pinned program/microcode/literal table and exact saved first-template boot words/heads. Freeze any one permitted heap-capacity enlargement before query; append only blanks to that band. Other nonboundary words/heads/capacities remain fixed.",
    "Independently compare every serialized input byte, including capacities, heads, boot heap/registers, stack markers, boundary payload and blank cells. expected_constructor/input_bytes are useful reviewed independent helpers, but hashes alone cannot replace decoded correspondence.",
    "Launch from the true parser start, not the semantic entry; record exact step limit and actual complete outcome. Native accepted status must correspond to the pinned accept state and every final head inside its declared band.",
    "Bind complete final output bytes, machine state, transition counters and trace digest. A later separately owned independent interpreter replay must use the same full input, code and limit and compare all final output bytes; a digest or cropped patch alone is insufficient.",
    "Review fresh runtime/toolchain/worker/owner boundaries with full compilation and query costs, direct child reaping and complete caller terminal clock. Old proof-worker leaf source evidence does not cover compiler/native subprocess descendants. Old native transport/resource receipt is historical and is not a fresh accepted wrapper.",
    "Resource cutoff, cancellation, compile failure or missing owned terminal remains UNKNOWN. A completed producer native query is pending independent replay and owned resource acceptance, not final native certificate acceptance."
  ],
  "compatibility_argument": [
    "fol_checker.tree main invokes proof(request.proof,target,None,registry,theory); a local assumption index has no top-level Gamma and is incompatible without an adapter.",
    "A compatible forward reduction appends exactly hypothesis-0, hypothesis-1, hypothesis-2 named CLOSED axioms equal to the three ordered source hypotheses; all original signature/axiom/schema values remain unchanged.",
    "Only the three assumption command kinds/parameter fields change to axiom plus the corresponding occurrence name. Every formula, other 21 complete commands, all 24 row positions and prior MP indices remain unchanged.",
    "Native acceptance is for the extended theory. The original sequent and exact occurrence mapping must be bound separately; this does not emit a deduction-theorem proof or universal closure.",
    "All rules used by the saved certificate occur in the fixed checker: axiom, instantiate, eq_subst, mp, plus the assumption-to-axiom reduction. No generalize, induction or block command is used.",
    "Translation is checking a previously discovered proof, not another GCTS search, new proof discovery, learned proposal, or native tile search."
  ],
